# =============================================================================
# राज चौक — copy to `.env.local` (gitignored). NEVER put real secrets here.
#
# This MVP has NO application secrets. Cognito and AppSync credentials live
# only in the generated, gitignored `amplify_outputs.json`. If a secret is ever
# needed, it belongs in Amplify secret management and is consumed inside
# `amplify/` via `secret('NAME')` — never read from this file.
# =============================================================================

# ---- PUBLIC FRONTEND VARIABLES ----------------------------------------------
# Inlined into the browser bundle at build time. Assume everything here is
# world-readable, because it is. Validated by src/lib/env.ts at module load, so
# a bad value fails the build rather than producing wrong canonical URLs.

# No trailing slash — one produces `https://rajchowk.in//article/x` in every
# canonical link, which search engines index as a separate URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME=राज चौक
NEXT_PUBLIC_AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
# development | sandbox | staging | production
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENV=development

# ---- SERVER-SIDE / LOCAL DEV ONLY -------------------------------------------
# Never inlined into the browser bundle. Credentials come from ~/.aws, never
# from a file in the repository.
AWS_PROFILE=default
AWS_REGION=ap-south-1

# ---- SYNTH-TIME ESCAPE HATCHES ----------------------------------------------
# Read by amplify/backend.ts during CDK synth. Both are UNSET in every
# environment by default, and both exist to make a guard overridable rather
# than to be used routinely.
#
# Allows this one-model schema to deploy to branch main/production. The
# production stack of this Amplify app holds 25 models; deploying here without
# a data migration asks CloudFormation to delete 24 live tables. Read the
# comment in amplify/backend.ts before setting this.
# ALLOW_MINIMAL_ON_MAIN=1
#
# Allows synthesis outside ap-south-1. The application targets Mumbai for
# Indian readers; this exists for a deliberate multi-region experiment.
# ALLOW_ANY_REGION=1

# ---- E2E --------------------------------------------------------------------
E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Port for the Playwright-managed server. Both the server and baseURL derive
# from this, so changing it here is sufficient.
E2E_PORT=3000
# Set to 1 to skip Playwright's built-in webServer (e.g. testing a deployment).
# E2E_NO_SERVER=1

# ---- SECRETS ----------------------------------------------------------------
# None. Deliberately.
